  "publicationDraft": "Evans traded Jefferson and Patterson for Mike Williams, Conner and Robinson, addressing a struggling backfield without abandoning his receiving corps. Stew assembled Jefferson, Kupp and Diggs, then lost Patterson to knee surgery and Kupp to an ankle injury. Jefferson's historic 1,809-yard season kept the investment valuable. Evans wasn't exactly blessed with good health either: Conner missed three games with injured ribs, Williams hurt his ankle, and Robinson was flipped in October. The two packages returned remarkably similar raw starting points, but Jefferson delivered elite production in fewer lineup slots. Both managers had a plan; Stew bought a superstar while Evans bought depth that spent too much time in the damn medical tent.",
